# Navigation and Routing

Single navigation package and centralized route configuration.

## Mandatory rules

- Must use `go_router` only; definitions under `lib/app/router/`.
- Must use named routes or typed helpers; no scattered raw route strings.
- Must protect routes via guards using session and entitlements ([`permissions.mdc`](./permissions.mdc)).
- Must build navigation from union(role/module/user grants) ∩ subscription package ∩ assigned modules ∩ ABAC scope; omit unauthorized destinations from shell, drawer, rail, and menu bar.
- Deep links to unauthorized routes must redirect to localized forbidden/not-found states.
- Must use stable readable web URLs via `human_friendly_id` where resource IDs appear.
- Must not navigate in repositories or data sources.
- Must provide a localized not-found page for unknown routes.
- Should avoid unnecessary rebuilds in navigation shells; keep route transitions simple.
- Must reuse shell components from `frontend/lib/shared/layout/` for uniform navigation.
- Must localize all navigation labels, tooltips, and route titles.
- Must use design tokens exclusively; no hard-coded colors, spacing, or typography ([`design-system.mdc`](./design-system.mdc)).

## Shell rules

- Must use a shell route for persistent navigation.
- Mobile: bottom nav or drawer by destination count.
- Tablet: rail or compact side nav.
- Desktop/web: menu bar and side nav with collapse support.
- Must not duplicate pages for mobile/desktop unless interaction truly differs.

